commit.message:
Merge two-card batch default (owner choice a): two NVIDIA cards pipeline by default

Pipelined groups beat the serial default at 2 and 4 streams on 2x A6000 (+17/+22%) and 2x A4000 (+7..12/+17..20%);
one stream equal, -4% on A4000 IQ3_XXS. STRATA_BATCH_GROUPS_NV_SERIAL=1 or STRATA_DEFAULTS=026 gives serial.

layer-major prefill on a CUDA layer split: each stage runs its layers over the super-chunk and hands its rows to the next stage (#3976)

Problem: layer-major prefill declined every layer split, so a split model kept
re-reading each layer's streamed experts once per 8192-token chunk.

Changed:
- lm_prepare_chain sizes every stage with the same super-chunk (the smallest any
  stage fits, up to four rounds until they agree) and gives them back together;
- a stage runs only its layers [LB, LE); a later stage's rows arrive in its pinned
  R_host;
- a stage before the last writes its final rows into the next stage's R_host on
  the copy stream, then runs the next stage on a thread (std::async) while it reads
  its own next super-chunk. There is one hand-off buffer: a stage's final pass waits
  until the next stage has finished the previous super-chunk;
- layer_major_mid() asks the last stage, the one that reports the rows;
- run() drains the pipeline after the walk and clears the mid flag on every stage.

Not covered: only two stages were tried by the reporter (RTX 3060 + RTX 5060 Ti);
the peer-GPU tier and the stage helper have no layer-major form and decline.
